`h.f.write_all(..)` -- a method call whose receiver is a struct field on a
typed PARAMETER or local rather than on `self` -- dropped its receiver type
before the module slot was built, so every method-kind row in rust.yaml was
unreachable through it (INV-linub L3 residual). Shape A (self.f) shipped via
resolve_receiver_type, but that resolver is self-rooted only by contract.

Adds resolve_var_field_chain to the shared TreeSitterAnalyzer: root h ->
Holder via _var_types, field f -> File via the same struct field-type
registry -- the walk Go's _resolve_field_chain already does. Additive:
nothing else calls it, so the self-only path is unchanged; sets the module
SLOT only (never has_explicit_binding or resolved), so emission is
byte-identical and it cannot mint a first-party calls edge. Nine direct unit
tests cover every branch; the rust fixture's shape B moves from OPEN to
passing while shapes A/D/E hold as controls.

MEASURED CORPUS DELTA IS ZERO, reported not hidden. Edge-level A/B on
spacedrive (patch confirmed engaging by a 2,461x call trace): the walk
resolves 811 field chains, 0 io-boundary classifications change. The resolved
types are Option/Vec/String/HashMap/PathBuf/in-repo structs; the only
catalogued hit is Instant (host_info_read, not a sink). The field-receiver
write/lock/write_all sites here are on RwLock/Mutex/watcher fields, not
std::fs::File -- classifying them would be the false positives the item warned
of. Type-directed and correct-by-construction; the recoverable-and-catalogued-
sink subset is simply empty on this sample, and no genuine File write is
dropped (verified). This closes the STRUCTURE, matching shape A's ceiling-not-
payoff reporting.

